  "body": "I think there's an issue with the pipeTo() algorithm that prevents writing all the data. When the underlying source calls `close()` the state of the ReadableStream changes immediately to \"CLOSED\". If there is a `read()` on the readable ongoing at that point then pipeTo shutdown starts immediately, prohibiting the data that was read from being written to the WritableStream.\r\n\r\nI'm not 100% certain that this is a spec issue yet but I am making a note of it to look at it again later. I will close this bug if I conclude there is no actual issue.",
